No, truly, Ursula, she is too disdainful;
I know her spirits are as coy and wild
As haggards of the rock.

N.d., Sir George Young, translator, Sophocles, Oedipus Rex, 1991 Dover Publications edition, →ISBN, page 22,
Now am I hail-fellow-well-met with all;
Now every man gives me good-morrow;....

When lust doth rage it like a canker frets;
It topsie turvie, upside downe all sets;[…]
Where once it reigneth, there it maketh sure,
A man a harlot, and a wife a whoore;
